\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item The join is by STEM, case-insensitively, after mzLib removes MetaMorpheus's derivative suffixes (-calib, -averaged, in any order and number), so X-calib.mzML finds the row naming X.raw. A searched TAB acquired line overrides that rule for its file. A row whose stem joins nothing is tried once more by an earlier search's comment[searched data file].
\item Nothing else changes: no replicate or fraction is renumbered. comment[searched data file] goes directly after comment[data file]; an earlier search's is replaced, because it is this search's field.
\item A kept row shorter than the header is padded with empty cells, so the document is never ragged, unlike what sdrf read returns for the same file.
\item ambiguous: the other claimants of an acquisition get no row and are not in searched_without_row. shared_stem: the document can describe one run twice, and only the depositor can say which row is right.
\item The design verbs match searched files by exact name. Restrict first: sdrf design and sdrf isobaric-design key on comment[searched data file] when a document has it.
\item \code{--out} writes the whole document with CRLF line endings, whatever the input used, and mzLib adds .sdrf.tsv to a name that does not end in it. Name the file .sdrf.tsv.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
}
