\section{Not yet verified}{
The spec records these as open. They are listed rather than hidden:

\itemize{
\item PUSH-TO-MAINLAND: SdrfDocument.WriteResults returns nothing and adds .sdrf.tsv to a name not ending in it, so the bridge reports the path by mzLib's own test (ResultFile.CanRead) instead of being told. Ask mzLib to return the path written, or to refuse rather than rename. sdrf pool \code{--out} has the same rename and still reports the path as given.
\item No \code{--paths-stdin} form: stdin already carries the searched files, and one search restricts one SDRF.
\item SdrfSampleCopy (#1451, same PR) is not projected: it only feeds SdrfBuilder.Build, which is G-sdrf-verbs.
}
